{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-information-bandwidth","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:information-bandwidth","kind":"definition","title":"Information bandwidth per Planck time","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-information-speed-of-light","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-operational-entropy"],"tags":["information-bandwidth","information-theory","bremermann","speed-of-light","operational-entropy"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.informationBandwidth","text":"information-bandwidth.md","leanSource":"information-bandwidth.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:information-bandwidth\"></a><p>The <strong>information bandwidth</strong> per Planck time is the product of the <a href=\"#def:information-speed-of-light\" data-at=\"information-theory/speed-of-light\">speed of light</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_q</code> and the <a href=\"#def:operational-entropy\" data-at=\"information-theory/golden-julia-dynamics\">operational entropy</a> per fibre:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{B}(q)\n  = c_q \\cdot n_R(q) \\cdot \\eta_q\n  = \\frac{\\eta_q}{\\hbar_q \\cdot (q-1)}\n  = \\frac{\\eta_q}{q^{-1}(q-1)^2}\n  = \\frac{q \\cdot \\eta_q}{(q-1)^2}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-bandwidth.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.4.3","page":"b/def-information-bandwidth","qa":{"counts":{"pass":86,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":77},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Information.informationBandwidth","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-bandwidth.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
